{"name":"Electra","hex":"#55b492","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Electra","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Any of several mythical women, including a daughter of Agamemnon and Clytemnestra, one of the Pleiades, and one of the daughters of Oceanus and Tethys.","One of the stars in the Pleiades star cluster."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Electra"}],"entries":[{"title":"Electra","blocks":[{"text":"In Greek mythology Electra, also spelt Elektra, is a princess of Mycenae and the daughter of Agamemnon and Clytemnestra. Famously, Electra and her brother, Orestes, attack and kill Clytemnestra to avenge their father's murder."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Orestes_Electra_Python_MAN.jpg/330px-Orestes_Electra_Python_MAN.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electra"},{"title":"Electra (Sophocles play)","blocks":[{"text":"Electra, is a Greek tragedy by Sophocles. The original publication date is not known, but various stylistic similarities with the Philoctetes and the Oedipus at Colonus leads scholars to believe it was written towards the end of Sophocles' career. Richard Claverhouse Jebb dates it between 420 BC and 414 BC."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Electra_and_Orestes_-_Project_Gutenberg_eText_14994.png/330px-Electra_and_Orestes_-_Project_Gutenberg_eText_14994.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electra_(Sophocles_play)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Orestes_Elektra_Hermes_Louvre_K544.jpg/500px-Orestes_Elektra_Hermes_Louvre_K544.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Orestes_Elektra_Hermes_Louvre_K544.jpg/1280px-Orestes_Elektra_Hermes_Louvre_K544.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Orestes_Elektra_Hermes_Louvre_K544.jpg/500px-Orestes_Elektra_Hermes_Louvre_K544.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Orestes, Electra and Hermes at the tomb of Agamemnon, lucanian red-figure pelike, c. 380–370 BC, Louvre (K 544)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOrestes_Elektra_Hermes_Louvre_K544.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Toneel%2C_SFA022826804.jpg/500px-Toneel%2C_SFA022826804.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Toneel%2C_SFA022826804.jpg/1280px-Toneel%2C_SFA022826804.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Toneel%2C_SFA022826804.jpg/500px-Toneel%2C_SFA022826804.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dutch actress Marie Hamel in costume as Clytemnestra (1920)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AToneel%2C_SFA022826804.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Orestes_and_Electra_%284376294525%29.jpg/500px-Orestes_and_Electra_%284376294525%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Orestes_and_Electra_%284376294525%29.jpg/500px-Orestes_and_Electra_%284376294525%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Statue of Orestes and Electra, National Museum, Rome","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOrestes_and_Electra_(4376294525).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/P3085052_%284418793179%29.jpg/500px-P3085052_%284418793179%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm